{
  "case_id": "2008-07-542",
  "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MAZIARZ: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: More than 27 years ago in Belton this Court applied its prior decisions in Chimel and Robinson to the arrest of a recent occupant of an automobile. The Court sought to forge a workable straightforward rule that could be easily applied and predictably enforced by law enforcement officers in the field in this dangerous and dynamic situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MAZIARZ: In -- in our reply brief we pointed out in 2007 there were 93 reported cases where arrestees cuffed in the back of a patrol car escaped. So it -- it's very possible this could happen. Now, you have to know --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I take it you agree it's perfectly workable to say that if the defendant has been taken to the police station, they can't then search the car --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Are you more concerned about the ability to search the vehicle or the protection of the officer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. YANG",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Well, certainly the protection of the officer is what motivates the doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You've arrested this guy for -- for reckless driving. He was going 25 miles over the speed limit, okay? And you're going to search his car for evidence? Of what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. YANG",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Oh, no; when a suspect is put under custodial arrest, the -- there is increased incentive both to escape, to get weapons, and also to destroy any incriminating evidence that might be --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I -- I mean I don't know if it can go off on that. The -- it seems to me I -- I thought when I looked through this, which was quickly, it seemed to me everyone was assuming that it's contemporaneous. Of course, if it isn't contemporaneous, that's a new world, and maybe you would win on that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What does contemporaneous have to do with officer safety? It has to do with timing doesn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-56c941340668-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well are you saying do you have any in my own mind perhaps differently from you I think that the stare decisus is really brought into play when you think the earlier decision was wrong."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-542",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
